relational-operators-reject-strings — < <= > >= must order strings, not return nil
================================================================================

See also:
  - clautolisp/autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp, `numeric-order-p`
    (used by `builtin-<`, `builtin-<=`, `builtin->`, `builtin->=`).
  - issues/closed/autolisp-spec-comparison-operators-chapter-placement.issue
    (records that `<` `<=` `>` `>=` order strings lexicographically, per host).
  - issues/closed/strict-dialect-autolisp-divergences.issue §2 (the nil-folding
    of non-numeric arguments that `numeric-order-p` implements).

Context
-------

Found 2026-09-24 while factoring the SCHMS+/SCHME+ test harness into
outils-autolisp/autolisp-test/test-runner.lsp: `tu:load-all` must load files
in lexicographic order, and `(vl-sort paths '<)` left the list unsorted under
clautolisp 2.2.85. The harness now carries its own `tu:string<` as a
workaround.

AutoCAD and BricsCAD accept strings in the relational operators and compare
them character by character: `(< "a" "b")` is T. clautolisp's
`numeric-order-p` returns nil as soon as one argument is not a number, so
every string comparison is nil. VL-SORT with `'<` or `'>` (a very common
idiom to sort strings) then leaves the list unchanged.

Minimal reproduction
--------------------

With clautolisp 2.2.85, any dialect (checked with bricscad-v26 and strict):

    (< "a" "b")                      ; => nil     expected T
    (> "b" "a")                      ; => nil     expected T
    (vl-sort '("b" "a" "c") '<)      ; => ("b" "a" "c")  expected ("a" "b" "c")

Expected behaviour
------------------

- When all arguments are strings, compare them pairwise by character codes
  (the AutoCAD documentation: "the comparison is based on the numeric value
  of the characters"), shorter prefix first.
- Keep the current nil-folding for nil and other non-numeric, non-string
  arguments (loop-guard idiom `(<= 48 (car chars) 57)`).
- To verify on real hosts before fixing: mixed number/string arguments, and
  whether the comparison is by code point or by host codepage byte for
  non-ASCII characters.

* Resolved (already fixed in clautolisp 2.2.90; closed 2026-11-04)

Filed against 2.2.85 and re-added to issues/open/ on 2026-11-04, but the
fix had already shipped: comparison-operators-vendor-semantics (clautolisp
2.2.90 / spec 0.14.0, issues/closed/) made = /= < <= > >= follow AutoCAD
and BricsCAD, strings compared by character codes. Rechecked with the
installed 2.3.81, --dialect strict:

: (list (< "a" "b") (> "b" "a") (vl-sort (list "b" "a" "c") '<)
:       (<= "a" "a") (>= "b" "a" "a") (< "ab" "abc"))
: => (T T ("a" "b" "c") T T T)

Regression coverage: builtin-tests.lisp (the (< "a" "b") / (= "a" "b")
case near l. 7627). The SCHMS+/SCHME+ harness's tu:string< workaround can
be dropped.
